Z||000000||NSUMEY||04-25-2001||09:31 AM||||I haven't got my manual yet....can anyone tell me the rocker arm bolt torque spec? 84 L4 with roller rockers....may be a newer engine, perhaps replaced at one time because I didn't think rollers were introduced in the L4 until 85||||reg||5
Z||000001||85Josh||04-25-2001||11:47 AM||||Roller ROCKERS?! If you really mean rockers, then someone has put in aftermarket parts, and you'll have to figure out the manufacturer and call them. If you are referring to the roller LIFTERS that came on 86-up dukes,the Haynes book says 24 ft-lbs for 86-88, the earlier flat tappet engines use 20 ft-lbs.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000002||NSUMEY||04-25-2001||01:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85Josh:<BR><B>Roller ROCKERS?! If you really mean rockers, then someone has put in aftermarket parts, and you'll have to figure out the manufacturer and call them. If you are referring to the roller LIFTERS that came on 86-up dukes,the Haynes book says 24 ft-lbs for 86-88, the earlier flat tappet engines use 20 ft-lbs.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>oops...I meant roller lifters....got the spec for it....thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-25-2001||07:32 PM||||If the valve seat was altered then the rocker nut torque isn't your only issue.<P>If the seats have receeded into the head then the valves are sticking up higher on top. In that case you likely need shorter push rods than stock or spacers for under the rocker nuts.||||reg||1
